#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cdf

#% text
# `cdf(d, x)` gives the distribution function of `d`: the probability `P(X <= x)`. A list `x` gives a list of values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
cdf(normal_distribution(0, 1), 1.96)
#% output
#= 0.9750021048517795

#% cell
cdf(exponential_distribution(l), x)
#% output
#= piecewise([[1 - exp(-l*x), x >= 0]], 0)

#% cell
cdf(binomial_distribution(5, 1/2), 2)
#% output
#= 1/2

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The probability of an interval:

#% cell
n(cdf(normal_distribution(0, 1), 1) - cdf(normal_distribution(0, 1), -1))
#% output
#= 0.6826894921370859

